From 22a3cd208fe7968afb10a43295f4e1c6d28a322e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 00:09:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] (be) ob-kill60 libunwind capture_into_slot + phase-2
 hooks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the variant TU `be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_ob_kill60.cpp`.
Defines the three variant entry points the patch 0001 hooks call into:

  capture_into_slot
    libunwind walk seeded from the interrupted thread's saved
    `ucontext_t`. `unw_init_local2(..., UNW_INIT_SIGNAL_FRAME)` so
    the first IP read returns the interrupted PC, not the handler's
    own frame. Loop walks via `unw_get_reg(UNW_REG_IP)` + `unw_step`
    up to `kMaxSignalFrames`. Same shape as
    `print_stack_ck_phdr_unwind.cpp`.

  variant_wait_for_release
    Blocks the handler on `g_handler_release_pipe_rw[0]` via `poll`
    bounded by `kPipeReadTimeoutMs`. Drains reads whose sequence
    does not match (stale wakeups from prior dumps' late drains).
    Returns on match, on timeout, or on read failure — never hangs
    the handler indefinitely.

  variant_after_slot_read
    One `write` of the sequence on `g_handler_release_pipe_rw[1]`
    from the coordinator after copying the slot.

No `hasPHDRCache()` gate. ob-kill60 deliberately ships no PHDR cache
override; `unw_step` reaches libc `dl_iterate_phdr`, which takes the
loader lock and is not async-signal-safe. OceanBase ships this exact
shape in production; the variant inherits the risk so the report's
comparison against ck-phdr-unwind stays clean. The dlopen-deadlock
window is documented in docs/design/ob.md "Runtime dlopen / dlclose
compatibility".

`UNW_LOCAL_ONLY` is defined before `<libunwind.h>` so the include
resolves to the local-only `_ULx86_64_*` symbols the Doris libunwind
archive exports. `be/src/service/CMakeLists.txt` globs `*.cpp`
recursively, so the new TU is picked up without a CMakeLists edit.

Spec: docs/architecture.md "Layer 3d"; docs/design/ob.md "Decisions",
      "Steps".
Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_libunwind.c:55-82
  (`get_stack_trace_inplace` is the unwind loop shape ob-kill60
  transcribes; the seed differs — ob-kill60 uses the saved ucontext,
  OB uses `unw_getcontext`).

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
